// XFAIL: RT-468b: (RT-468, a shift) `A = 1 << 40` in a `#[repr(i64)]` enum is refused at -O0 ("this constant expression overflows") and is 256 at -O2 (an i32 shift by 40 mod 32); rustc prints 1099511627776 (0.30.2)
// From the re-review of the integer-literal work (t302int). Since v0.30.1 at least.
// EXPECT: 1099511627776
#[repr(i64)]
enum E { A = 1 << 40 }

fn main() {
    println("{}", E::A as i64);
}
